{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfxuqi9F1QSB9nk7DBNPf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done. The rule was created disabled, so I enabled it, and reading it back shows it enabled with status ok.\n\n- **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" has the time field `timestamp`.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-4fd1ccbb Web logs\" has two panels, \"Requests over time\" and \"Requests by response code\".\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-4fd1ccbb 5xx errors\" runs every minute and fires when more than 10 requests have a response code from 500 to 599 within 5 minutes. The `response` field is a string, so the query is a string range from \"500\" to \"599\" on `response.keyword`. That covers every 5xx code as long as the codes are three digits. I haven't checked that the query returns any hits.\n- **Panel edit:** I renamed the response-code panel to \"Responses by code\" and confirmed the new title on the dashboard.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":20805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":539},"output_tokens":325,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"fc33eb3b-3972-4037-a1d7-be64139ba56b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:41:04.458Z","request_id":"req_011CfxuqhvatD9m2aCUbEteK"}
